  "id": "Compound::DB01095 - Gene::3156",
  "verbalization": "Fluvastatin and Hmgcr are linked through a shared mechanism of action involving the inhibition of Hmg-Coa reductase, a key enzyme in cholesterol synthesis. The evidence suggests that Fluvastatin, as a statin, directly binds to Hmgcr, which is consistent across multiple paths. The observed relationship is reinforced by the fact that Fluvastatin causes the presence of myoglobin in urine and facial paresis, both of which are associated with Rosuvastatin and Pravastatin, which also bind to Hmgcr. This indicates a broader pharmacological profile where Fluvastatin, as a statin, exerts its effects through a common target, Hmgcr, and its downstream effects are mediated by the inhibition of this enzyme. The integration of these paths highlights the central role of Hmgcr in the pharmacological action of statins, with Fluvastatin serving as a representative of this class.",
